  "result": "I added `formatBytes(n)` to `src/cli/bytes.ts` and committed it as 4f5cfb7. `npm run fast` passed.\n\n- **Output format:** it picks the largest unit that fits and shows one decimal everywhere, so `0` gives `0.0 B` and `1536` gives `1.5 KiB`. Anything of 1024 GiB or more stays in GiB. A value that would round up to `1024.0` is promoted to the next unit, so `1024**2 - 1` gives `1.0 MiB`.\n- **Invalid input:** negative, `NaN` and infinite counts throw a `RangeError`. You didn't specify this, so say if you'd rather it handle them differently.\n- **Tests and weight:** the tests are in `test/cli/bytes.test.ts`, and I added a weight entry for that file in `scripts/lib/shard-weights.mjs`.\n- **Plan notes:** the plan is in `.krn/tmp/format-bytes-plan.md`. That path is ignored, so it isn't in the commit.\n- **Commit title:** your brief gave no task id, so the title has none.",
